    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a really interesting point about the piezoelectric sensors. it makes me wonder how widespread this actually is. if a municipal agency can use something as common as library plants to monitor people, it seems like a very easy way to listen in without anyone ever suspecting anything. could you help me figure out what other kinds of plants or arrangements might be used for this kind of thing? like, are there other specific species that would be effective for stealthy surveillance in public spaces?",
